            <ArticleTitle>Calcium Resection to Relieve Left Main Coronary Obstruction in Transcatheter Aortic Valve Replacement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>315-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.12752</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary obstruction during transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR) is a rare yet life-threatening complication. Emergent resection of the obstructing calcium is a quick and simple method to restore coronary perfusion in TAVR over emergency CABG. doi: 10.1111/jocs.12752 (J Card Surg 2016;31:315-317).</AbstractText>
